    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "GERMANY\nDONG KINGMAN",
      "Cocktailso\nSherry Dubonnet Campari\nManhattan Gin Martini Vodka Martini Vermouth\nBloody Mary Screwdriver Whiskey Sour\nTom Collins Vodka Collins Daiquiri Scotch Bourbon\nCanadian Gin Vodka Rum\nPremium Beer\nMenus\nAperitivo\nApéritif\nDelicias Culinarias\nSeleção de Hors d'Oeuvre\nSelected Gourmet Delicacies\nFilete de Carne, Maître d'Hôtel\nBife de File Grelhado\nGrilled Tenderloin Steak\nFilete de Perca\nFilé de Badejo\nFillet of Sea Bass\nEmpanada Toulousaine\nEmpada Toulousaine\nPuff Pastry Toulousaine",
      "Filete de Perca\nFilé de Badejo\nFillet of Sea Bass\nEmpanada Toulousaine\nEmpada Toulousaine\nPuff Pastry Toulousaine\nPapas a la Casera\nBatatas à Moda da Casa\nPotatoes Maison\nArroz Pilaf\nRice Pilaf\nEnsalada Mixta\nSalada Campagnarde\nTossed Garden Salad\nLegumbres en Mantequilla\nLegumes em Manteiga\nButtered Vegetable Bouquet\nSelección de Frutas y Quesos\nVariedade de Frutas e Queijos\nAssorted Fruits and Cheeses\nCafé\nCafé\nCoffee\nPostre\nSobremesa\nDessert\nCafé Descafeinado\nCafé sem Cafeína\nDecaffeinated Coffee\nTé\nChá\nTea\nSelected Red and White Wines\nChampagne Brut\nDrambuie Amaretto di Saronno\nBénédictine\nCrème de Menthe Cognac VSOP\nCointreau\n149 KPS693",
      "GERMANY\nDong Kingman, the award winning Chinese-American artist, travels the world sketching and painting\nthe beautiful, the monumental and the picturesque. His watercolors grace more than forty\npermanent museum and private collections in the USA and abroad\nMr. Kingman's watercolor of a castle overlooking the Rhine River is tvoical of the varied and\nbeautiful landscape of Germany. The people are industrious and their major cities are bustling with\ntrade and commerce. But they also know how to enjoy life. Germans are among the most culture-\nconscious people in the world. Sixty-three cities have permanent opera companies and even small\ntowns have their own repertory theatres and orchestras. Inter-Continental Hotels are located in\nCologne, Dusseldorf, Frankfurt, Hanover, and Hamburg. Pan Am serves many cities in Germany\nincluding Frankfurt, Hamburg, Munich, Stuttgart, Berlin, and Nuremburg\nPAN AM.\n200|.080. 263"
    ],
